id "q-335392" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} - 2y = x^{2}e^{2x}$.\nSelect the correct options below.\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x) =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe general solution is given by $y(x) =$ {{field-2}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311586 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a488da-8074-50a9-ba1d-c7e0f32bf719" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308780} {:answer/id #uuid "64a5c638-4dbb-57eb-a6fb-248e76429030" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309522} {:answer/id #uuid "893e7fae-64e2-57b6-af19-e61e904ea8b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309829} {:answer/id #uuid "9e515d8a-f8c4-5ea9-9b59-674573d38b1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{C}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310026} {:answer/id #uuid "b92c0b6e-441f-5b77-9aa7-a8dc52625f53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04a488da-8074-50a9-ba1d-c7e0f32bf719" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308780} :answer-field/id #uuid "785b77fb-6634-5289-8f5e-c7972e2ca683" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "223e604f-882b-578c-9005-65a6a468f7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309006} {:answer/id #uuid "3a151fdc-c615-56f8-af30-2dacf342942e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309195} {:answer/id #uuid "7b511ce9-9c0e-54e8-8e7e-93916e342c24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309711} {:answer/id #uuid "ad26b27d-2be0-5935-829c-fe759d649c9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b511ce9-9c0e-54e8-8e7e-93916e342c24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309711} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c99e1a2-52bb-5b04-85f5-ed344de385bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311192}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d36870f2-83c3-53eb-b9c4-cfdc50550717" :question/math-academy-id "q-335409" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this integral, we integrate by parts. \n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int {u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nLet $u=x,{u}^{′}=1,{v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ and $v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2} & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =x(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311587 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24c590c3-891b-511b-9e8d-1e0317eac036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309024} {:answer/id #uuid "c4250262-bc93-5a7e-a34a-2623ae9d7561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310322} {:answer/id #uuid "c82f0da4-6a92-5001-89a2-66f34618a0ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310355} {:answer/id #uuid "ee20a83a-6373-5864-bf59-eeaad3c5fb28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4250262-bc93-5a7e-a34a-2623ae9d7561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310322} :answer-field/id #uuid "26833fad-1674-5264-a99a-1ab167ee5815" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34e87914-2491-5ea9-986c-2fa933b9f42e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309150} {:answer/id #uuid "93802e8a-2438-526b-9013-756c85306841" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}({e}^{x}+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309928} {:answer/id #uuid "cc68d1a8-cb75-5053-8d7d-c7bbccf33bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310385} {:answer/id #uuid "ce5f5849-731e-572b-9350-7951b8593415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}({e}^{x}+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34e87914-2491-5ea9-986c-2fa933b9f42e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309150} :answer-field/id #uuid "842dfce6-3596-5e08-aa3d-f4ed3e02c6ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311159}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "039312c7-7497-5736-bf10-d497d1c61328" :question/math-academy-id "q-335412" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{3}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (3/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{3}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y) & ={x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}\\cdot y & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{3})\\,dx & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & ={e}^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314755 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a701b78-2f7b-5869-a35c-a68265d84c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312297} {:answer/id #uuid "35b399dd-b281-56b7-8db7-a76855d06ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312408} {:answer/id #uuid "c01117c8-2cdb-582a-8d44-4d6c98807eb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313480} {:answer/id #uuid "e4465b0a-93ed-52f4-b50c-bf89f91e8717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4465b0a-93ed-52f4-b50c-bf89f91e8717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313777} :answer-field/id #uuid "619b5a02-9bcf-5c4e-9804-90020e919aba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b8ab38f-ccc9-5c4d-9953-e2511696a304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312314} {:answer/id #uuid "82438980-e317-5426-8c57-7d992347312f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313024} {:answer/id #uuid "a83c841e-df51-5c6e-b081-e26fb120e44e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313294} {:answer/id #uuid "ab3cf1a5-b0c2-595f-a092-5ea9a23fd911" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82438980-e317-5426-8c57-7d992347312f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313024} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5afcbd6-0c6a-5f61-91f9-74372beb0557" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314457}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f406ffe6-dbd4-575f-96ea-c90a9a6d9f11" :question/math-academy-id "q-339140" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y=7,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{5}{x}$ and $Q(x)=7.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (5/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{5})} \\\\  & ={x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{5}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y) & ={x}^{5}\\cdot 7 \\\\ {x}^{5}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5{x}^{4}y & =7{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{5})\\,dx & =\\int 7{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{5} & =\\frac{7{x}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391568 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bd0b65e-3a0f-5994-9689-9aef5b5c9454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{e}^{-x}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391570} {:answer/id #uuid "3fae5784-6514-5371-820c-1909539d4c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391571} {:answer/id #uuid "58c34fda-7cad-508d-a7f2-d8bf06c08b7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391572} {:answer/id #uuid "7448e8d2-a22f-59f6-bc6b-c65f6e7cf2de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7448e8d2-a22f-59f6-bc6b-c65f6e7cf2de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391573} :answer-field/id #uuid "d308949f-707a-5a2c-802c-a0a17c33433a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391569} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4e6cf3c-fccb-5029-b604-d1593b0daddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391575} {:answer/id #uuid "1e61f74a-48e8-542c-a33f-c9fe7a376f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391576} {:answer/id #uuid "74653977-5fc1-57a5-a3e9-24eb70eb33c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391577} {:answer/id #uuid "fb69fbee-2b0a-5d6f-b11d-267cf756dd9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74653977-5fc1-57a5-a3e9-24eb70eb33c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391577} :answer-field/id #uuid "2021aa17-0151-5e2d-987a-a1856edc5e53" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391574}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6530e5db-b521-5f5c-99f7-59872d852e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-335402" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=6{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is already in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-3$ and $Q(x)=6{e}^{2x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-3x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y) & ={e}^{-3x}\\cdot 6{e}^{2x} \\\\ {e}^{-3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{e}^{-3x}\\cdot y & =6{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x}) & =6{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-3x} & =-6{e}^{-x}+C \\\\ y & =-6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d5e5efa-0ad9-5cb1-8007-def75d4c0f34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391733} {:answer/id #uuid "181ce215-60ee-5a98-8d16-1f87a5c66bf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391734} {:answer/id #uuid "c201762a-3b3f-52e3-a4c2-6f449ab4bd0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391735} {:answer/id #uuid "45bdee38-54f6-5e18-9b5f-1f916081c4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45bdee38-54f6-5e18-9b5f-1f916081c4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391736} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52979ca-88b2-53be-b424-0a20f99bf0c6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391732} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02bcb740-d3b0-5e03-ac52-deeb78de3ac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391738} {:answer/id #uuid "0f0496f9-803e-5f66-af97-d84ac1ef5ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391739} {:answer/id #uuid "917a7312-27b6-560b-80be-1afb23076cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391740} {:answer/id #uuid "94fc55df-9a81-5694-9adb-ccac511991c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94fc55df-9a81-5694-9adb-ccac511991c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391741} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e39085e-c8a9-5cbc-b6d2-646a14b27243" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391737}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08d92346-a7e8-58c6-8d60-e4702d743dd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-339138" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=x{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-3$ and $Q(x)=x{e}^{3x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-3x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y) & ={e}^{-3x}\\cdot x{e}^{3x} \\\\ {e}^{-3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{e}^{-3x}\\cdot y & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x}) & =x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-3x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435866 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21b04f8f-b31f-5e1d-8a4e-18caced2e9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435836} {:answer/id #uuid "8bb32a9a-ce7c-5dfe-90c1-5f241762ceee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435842} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf9a5e7-9387-5f18-9a2c-3d8174e2d646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435852} {:answer/id #uuid "f669873b-95d4-589e-957f-2bb522268738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21b04f8f-b31f-5e1d-8a4e-18caced2e9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435836} :answer-field/id #uuid "054a463e-8111-5ef5-af3f-4d0babd67edf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435861} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "856f41fb-43dc-578b-9457-c64453f94455" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435840} {:answer/id #uuid "96612919-8760-51a3-a0ec-f59a5ea738c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435844} {:answer/id #uuid "a91ab2dc-5a5e-503c-8f55-0ebae59165d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435848} {:answer/id #uuid "cceac854-6bb0-51ac-8a27-c1be3b7727f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "856f41fb-43dc-578b-9457-c64453f94455" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435840} :answer-field/id #uuid "658b2e4e-a8cb-5de8-9ced-3ee2b6b96997" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435862}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "536cae39-f031-5c30-a8b0-a9b62b8632a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-339139" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y=5,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{4}{x}$ and $Q(x)=5.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (4/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{4}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y) & ={x}^{4}\\cdot 5 \\\\ {x}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{x}^{3}y & =5{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{4})\\,dx & =\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{4} & ={x}^{5}+C \\\\ y & =x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Integrating Factors"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087879 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087454 :question/id #uuid "09d09b0b-2132-59b2-9eb9-ae0748f09252" :question/math-academy-id "e-21743" :question/problem "Solve the following initial value problem using the method of integrating factors.\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + 3x^2y = 9x^2, \\qquad y(0) = 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)y = Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x) = 3x^2$ and $Q(x) = 9x^2.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x) = e^{x^3}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 9{x}^{2} \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot y & =9{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{3}}) & =9{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u = x^3{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{3}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 9{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{3}} & =\\int 3{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{3}} & =3{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{3}} & =3{e}^{{x}^{3}}+C \\\\ y & =3+C{e}^{-{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0) = 1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3+C{e}^{-{0}^{3}} \\\\ 1 & =3+C \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny = 3 - 2e^{-x^3}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01c5809f-cb10-5192-b646-13036813137d" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84c716b1-12e1-584c-a0e8-f70e89466844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085479} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4b135f-e7b1-52e4-98b6-841574f71fb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085480} {:answer/id #uuid "c6fa3cf4-3e3b-5bd9-abc1-0715b68ebf64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085481} {:answer/id #uuid "fc090ec4-b599-5fc5-ac32-5c9b976c5883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085482}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a4c16bb1-0664-5e29-99cf-d582a29f1061" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085478} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1e7012e-39ed-52b9-9d95-96083e910119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - 4e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085484} {:answer/id #uuid "adcabf4f-fde7-5d05-982b-9bb7d12516dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{4}{e^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085485} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc943f9-fad2-5dd7-91c8-2d1a422cac8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085486} {:answer/id #uuid "6ae2fca2-1a66-56a2-99b7-16089b2e1046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e^{x}} - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085487} {:answer/id #uuid "795a684e-06f0-5304-a914-f1ce23a39093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{e^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085488}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8a96d149-1d03-5c69-9f3f-93f3d2996138" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085483}] :question/id #uuid "9213a6d1-eed0-504f-8fac-112369977a1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-334916" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} + y = 1, y(0) =-3$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x) =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x) =$ {{field-2}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088144 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42485b83-5931-53b1-8e35-f51001ba1f8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435839} {:answer/id #uuid "9ffccaf5-41e6-5e01-a737-ef5c5c68550a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435846} {:answer/id #uuid "d15343f4-d7a9-5b07-861f-21158d88cd11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435855} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b3ee9d-6980-58f8-a0f9-f8fb1fe2f5f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435856} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d4fe97-8780-56b9-9818-a1be81f11d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8b3ee9d-6980-58f8-a0f9-f8fb1fe2f5f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435856} :answer-field/id #uuid "3037a011-e9f1-5dab-aa7d-6ffe3d4faaec" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085509} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f03f76b8-d043-505d-8492-b243b8108a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085516} {:answer/id #uuid "8d866b2c-596b-59ce-a796-aa22c8b178ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435843} {:answer/id #uuid "ae550e0c-1776-5b97-ab81-e46cb204df85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435850} {:answer/id #uuid "fc50ddf9-0597-5079-a434-4f4d589089a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d866b2c-596b-59ce-a796-aa22c8b178ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435843} :answer-field/id #uuid "af75cec9-5a94-548e-88fa-c37d26f071ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085515}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8d9c75e9-1ee8-5d41-904e-f9bb375cf039" :question/math-academy-id "q-335808" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{2}\\cdot y=x,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $Q(x)=x.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (x/2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}/4}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{2}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\cdot y & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}) & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4})\\text{d}x & =\\int x{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} & =\\int 2{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} & =2{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/4} & =2{e}^{{x}^{2}/4}+C \\\\ y & =2+C{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2+C{e}^{-{0}^{2}/4} \\\\ 1 & =2+C \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088145 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "117ed42d-e3b1-523b-8f69-150942e554cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308872} {:answer/id #uuid "9d7fd74c-8a73-54ba-b5f8-00d9b9214cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310020} {:answer/id #uuid "e85590a8-371b-51ed-9363-5ee1c845dfb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310594} {:answer/id #uuid "eb8ce5eb-4f47-5650-a379-9985a81218f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb8ce5eb-4f47-5650-a379-9985a81218f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310621} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f85c8ef-b569-567a-8797-508841891ad6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311045} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dac0063-ecc2-5627-bb27-eec391f6c6f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309090} {:answer/id #uuid "81429b38-817c-58d8-ba84-9a927f701049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309765} {:answer/id #uuid "cadb2780-5df9-5f0a-9927-a1da1d6dd3d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310373} {:answer/id #uuid "d4679384-5633-50c0-98ce-64a2bd94c291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81429b38-817c-58d8-ba84-9a927f701049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309765} :answer-field/id #uuid "f955a4ed-77cc-558d-8e88-a71d0a0707d4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311524}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7bd80c89-2759-5cf8-8ba7-8fb4c49482e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-335810" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\nx\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=4{x}^{2},\\,y(1)=2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The first step is to write the equation in standard form,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,.\n$$\n\nIn doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y & =4{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}(x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y) & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot 4{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y & =4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{2}{x},\\,Q(x)=4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 4x \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =4{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & ={x}^{4}+C \\\\ y & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(1)=2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & ={1}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{1}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =1+C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2217ec13-aeca-54c6-b184-b9c6f12eca21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309005} {:answer/id #uuid "278ab869-b3ab-5209-b251-49e30ed08f3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309045} {:answer/id #uuid "cb884bde-aa7d-5ea3-8269-75c1c85782d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310378} {:answer/id #uuid "e304072c-14d0-5b9a-91ef-e7c21ca3967c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb884bde-aa7d-5ea3-8269-75c1c85782d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310378} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d4b8151-a2dd-5d21-b3a8-5f1786ce72f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51d8ba46-b7ec-5aeb-9c2e-92c427b44105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309368} {:answer/id #uuid "6e835f28-6c17-5099-9e1d-5557f103db76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309601} {:answer/id #uuid "784a4e7f-4997-59d7-9dbf-2d44fdbb9535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309692} {:answer/id #uuid "88322c85-406a-50de-beb7-e95ff2a7c6e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309817} {:answer/id #uuid "f316da64-a8b2-5ef5-a90e-929545648a49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "784a4e7f-4997-59d7-9dbf-2d44fdbb9535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309692} :answer-field/id #uuid "9edac9dd-3740-53a2-adc8-4f1b9b142575" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311250}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb60ed14-2886-5407-9edd-93c36aa77da2" :question/math-academy-id "q-335811" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2y}{x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}},\\,y(\\pi )=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}.$ \n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(\\pi )=0$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\pi ) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+C}{{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{C}{{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48e70df3-e69a-52ce-adaf-9d80576fc124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309306} {:answer/id #uuid "4de60ca3-08eb-5908-84e7-337d050635cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309339} {:answer/id #uuid "60127d29-07b2-5438-b25c-538c97234290" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309472} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e91b0c-4363-5464-927a-584f15d25ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310236} {:answer/id #uuid "e373d4bf-5114-5201-a0ca-5837cf70ed2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7e91b0c-4363-5464-927a-584f15d25ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310236} :answer-field/id #uuid "964f9aee-69e3-5eaf-ba62-46327eb55e3f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd4c10d-4104-533e-a7ea-701ca41dc419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309354} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab118d1-7dd3-5f85-b172-3299a04f369d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309705} {:answer/id #uuid "976ecd48-d13c-560a-802a-8e7cf948da05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309962} {:answer/id #uuid "de8dc48e-6d1c-5472-ac5b-8b94b9419130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "976ecd48-d13c-560a-802a-8e7cf948da05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309962} :answer-field/id #uuid "fba4b49a-a123-5ea4-a04f-61aaf7f9c4c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311533}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3bbe03fd-0d2c-564c-9b93-a7997b3f7696" :question/math-academy-id "q-335812" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x},\\,x>0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y) & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ yx & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{2C}{\\pi } \\\\ C & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bb9195b-384d-5b2f-bad0-6dd43e0f4b44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391595} {:answer/id #uuid "f34ac63a-04a2-52a7-a90f-f8f4d8d09299" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391596} {:answer/id #uuid "2d29d24c-fd03-58f5-91b9-3629bcaeee91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391597} {:answer/id #uuid "f585add5-def6-5238-932b-3a30184083f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391598} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f4e1e7-75e7-58c7-87b8-4747684ab781" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3f4e1e7-75e7-58c7-87b8-4747684ab781" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391599} :answer-field/id #uuid "7806b0bb-9404-54a9-9afe-9fe5aae500c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d49da7f-4559-53d4-88e7-a4a538e83bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391601} {:answer/id #uuid "185130ca-9e63-5f95-8858-fbe1360a02af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391602} {:answer/id #uuid "24752170-0362-5a79-8550-d496d2deb223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391603} {:answer/id #uuid "7644849e-bdfd-532f-b35d-2dd327bd7b3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d49da7f-4559-53d4-88e7-a4a538e83bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391601} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a5f76ae-1afb-592e-a102-26dd10e20b42" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391600}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c6ef87c-1a0b-5973-8a1d-74f719874948" :question/math-academy-id "q-335806" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=2x{e}^{-x},\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=2x{e}^{-x}.$ \n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 2x{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{x}y & =2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x}) & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{x} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ y & =({x}^{2}+C){e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =({0}^{2}+C){e}^{-0} \\\\ -2 & =(0+C)\\cdot 1 \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c71556-c8bb-509e-b7b6-813b830221cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391607} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc0fd51-b3d5-5b60-822b-55ce1a39a048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391608} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5f9c6d-a3bd-55c8-a595-021440af2d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-5{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391609} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff86545-6fe9-59ce-a43b-d596ae985d85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391610} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e86c18-962f-5498-8cd8-fd15eaf09b4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13c71556-c8bb-509e-b7b6-813b830221cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391607} :answer-field/id #uuid "75c53fba-addc-5347-89bc-46926b4cec8a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68eff5b7-73e9-589d-b262-8718bbf64cfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391613} {:answer/id #uuid "708406f2-8554-5163-8a8c-780da5f0a24e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391614} {:answer/id #uuid "38c2efa8-509c-59df-90e0-5ff1a247796d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391615} {:answer/id #uuid "878ffcb1-ce95-5b25-bcf5-982716631d15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38c2efa8-509c-59df-90e0-5ff1a247796d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391615} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0dfecd2-1e22-5e5a-aff3-e35469e93c9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391612}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cba95378-fbb4-59fe-bb7c-3f501d3e7ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-335829" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=8,\\,y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=4$ and $Q(x)=8.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{4x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y) & ={e}^{4x}\\cdot 8 \\\\ {e}^{4x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{4x}\\cdot y & =8{e}^{4x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x}) & =8{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 8{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =8(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x})+C \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =2{e}^{4x}+C \\\\ y & =2+C{e}^{-4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2+C{e}^{-4(0)} \\\\ -1 & =2+C(1) \\\\ C & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2-3{e}^{-4x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397296 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c73a7b2-a2bf-518a-beb1-31fbbadf0c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397298} {:answer/id #uuid "d70f278f-f71b-563b-90a5-a72e4490f97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397299} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9aa96a-e438-54ed-91f2-a9cd9b89c2af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397300} {:answer/id #uuid "be7b681a-d4b7-5605-ba2e-22acaaed6363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397301} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0d3cd9-78d0-5801-b268-5ffd73ca96c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e0d3cd9-78d0-5801-b268-5ffd73ca96c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397302} :answer-field/id #uuid "40c6d291-cf90-51ae-b2e3-e5400146213f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397297} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e829349-3bd7-53b1-81eb-45b5da9870a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{12x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397304} {:answer/id #uuid "ddaeb121-e0a6-501b-9a51-af6c7d17b5d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397305} {:answer/id #uuid "831b7918-1f4b-50de-b1bd-28a0091624cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397306} {:answer/id #uuid "327e9b36-504a-55cd-bdeb-9a295dbac872" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "327e9b36-504a-55cd-bdeb-9a295dbac872" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397307} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1cc20f5-acca-5b79-8f90-bd4ac033d4c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397303}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b18cb65d-b781-5075-91bf-6c656ac3ed30" :question/math-academy-id "q-339145" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y=x,\\,y(0)=5\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $Q(x)=x.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (x/6)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot y & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}) & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12})\\text{d}x & =\\int x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =\\int 6{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}+C \\\\ y & =6+C{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=5$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =6+C{e}^{-{0}^{2}/12} \\\\ 5 & =6+C \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d921686-f16a-5dba-8a57-bf18cea65de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}(1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435834} {:answer/id #uuid "21b21254-3e18-5695-9053-f6ca9ce7117b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-2x}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435837} {:answer/id #uuid "ae129e42-b937-59e5-976e-b7f0a9bd2526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(5-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435849} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7b3997-dd21-54f1-8bae-4ea74ec54405" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(3+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435854} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b016d8-b939-5406-bcfa-caab3f97d6bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae129e42-b937-59e5-976e-b7f0a9bd2526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(5-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435849} :answer-field/id #uuid "872a01bb-a58c-517b-8a38-5d170114d390" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435864} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0249902f-f26e-5a08-91d2-72b3ea108e58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435831} {:answer/id #uuid "12775c73-4492-5f55-9c3e-64f7ff76cc43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435833} {:answer/id #uuid "89b946b2-2ff0-52e9-9809-36bbebc85401" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435841} {:answer/id #uuid "b2373707-12f6-5094-9104-60d956b3f32f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0249902f-f26e-5a08-91d2-72b3ea108e58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435831} :answer-field/id #uuid "db6d7e71-81cf-5a3b-b7fa-5481d846b976" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435865}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb095d57-a547-5e39-b061-eaeaefb98858" :question/math-academy-id "q-335830" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(0)=4\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-2$ and $Q(x)={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{-2x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y) & ={e}^{-2x}\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {e}^{-2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2{e}^{-2x}\\cdot y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-2x}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-2x} & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ y & ={e}^{2x}(C-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=4$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & ={e}^{2(0)}(C-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\ 4 & =C-1 \\\\ C & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{2x}(5-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Integrating Factors"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092217 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092059 :question/id #uuid "bc48e845-b2a7-5e30-9c73-b7d842f4090c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5383" :question/problem "The point $P$ has polar coordinates $\\left( 6,\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} \\right).$ Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P.$" :question/worked-solution "To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx = r\\cos\\theta, \\qquad y=r\\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tx &= r\\cos\\theta\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} \\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2}\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 3\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\ty &= r\\sin\\theta\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} \\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\cdot \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 3\\sqrt{3}\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $\\left(3, 3\\sqrt{3}\\right).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f65d032-9acc-5fe6-b7c2-b8293576cb4c" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5754374-bb37-57a0-9738-e72c3a15a78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2\\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091337} {:answer/id #uuid "db6ea619-9642-5828-a198-c1c869433a14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091338} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2db77a-c458-568d-b8c8-b9aa49a12720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091339} {:answer/id #uuid "e6874207-a8db-5b0c-846e-01c6acc30c97" :an